135	/**
136	 * Every site the customer owns, in the exact shape the card renders.
137	 *
138	 * Four reads, one round of parallelism, all scoped to project ids this user
139	 * owns (the first query is the authorization boundary; the rest filter by its
140	 * output). None of them is per-card — an N+1 over a site list is how a
141	 * dashboard becomes slow the moment someone is actually using the product.
